.support_cursor

## Personal working notes an agent keeps about the person whose data it's
## working on, in whichever project. Private per checkout and never committed:
## these repos shouldn't carry one person's notes around, and in sage the file
## holds a production API token. One per checkout — a second learner gets their
## own clone rather than a second file here.

USER.md

## Anything this project alone needs ignored. Everything above is shared, so
## an entry added there quietly ignores the same path in every Chatwing
## project — which is how a recipe app ended up ignoring a Japanese learner's
## notes, and a language app ended up ignoring a video-eval corpus it has no
## concept of.

# @chatwing:projectIgnores:start

## Miks runtime state when MIKS_HOME points inside the repo (tests, dev).

.miks/

## Release credentials (NOTARY_PROFILE and friends) for `yarn release`.

.env.release.local

## Neo mirro script
mirror-to-neo.sh

# @chatwing:projectIgnores:end
